          "item": {
            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "AI helped Shenzhen judges handle 50% more cases in 2025 and will now expand to dozens of Chinese cities",
            "articleSection": "Daily Utility",
            "abstract": "Judges at Shenzhen's Intermediate People's Court processed 50 percent more cases in 2025 compared to 2024, with each judge handling an average of 744 cases — up by 249 — after deploying a pilot AI-powered case management system. The court has announced the system will now be rolled out to dozens of additional Chinese cities. The development marks one of the most concrete large-scale deployments of AI in a national judicial system, raising both efficiency and due-process questions.",
            "url": "https://www.scmp.com/news/china/politics/article/3352161/ai-helped-shenzhen-judges-handle-cases-50-faster-future-china",
            "publisher": {
